  editing the shared guideline doc and choosing width values nobody has reviewed. That wasn't in the approved design, so
  I'm checking before I do it.

  The real difference between the options is whether the spec doc changes.

  - [1mAdd the tokens to 01 first.[0m This would be a new [38;5;153mdocs:[39m commit, so three commits instead of two. I'd add:
    - control heights of 1.75, 2.25 and 2.75rem, taken from 02's 28, 36 and 44px;
    - field widths I'd propose: xs 6rem, sm 10rem, md 16rem, lg 24rem;
    - colours for the secondary Button and the accent Tag, using only existing tokens. The accent Tag would use
      [38;5;153m--accent-subtle[39m with [38;5;153m--info-text[39m, the same pairing banners already use.

    The page CSS would then reference only tokens, so it would hold up to the line-by-line review. The cost is that
    reviewers also have to approve the new token values, and later changes to them affect every page.
  - [1mMake no new tokens.[0m Height would come from the input padding plus line height (about 36px, not exactly), and widths
    from [38;5;153mcalc()[39m on spacing tokens. The spec stays untouched, but the sizes are approximate. A reviewer could also read
    the [38;5;153mcalc[39m multiples as raw sizes in disguise and ask for another review round.
  - [1mWait for the design-system owner.[0m You'd ask them for the official values. Nothing is guessed, but the work is
    blocked until they answer.

  I recommend adding the tokens to 01. It's what 01 itself says to do, and it keeps the page CSS free of anything a
  reviewer would flag.
